_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 32
---
order: 32
---
short_label: XI.32
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Parallelepipedal solids which are of the same height are to one another as their bases.
----
proof:

Let {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} be parallelepipedal solids of the same height.

I say that the parallelepipedal solids {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} are to one another as their bases, that is, that the solid {AB|sAB} to the solid {CD|sCD} as the base {AE|pAE} is to the base {CF|pCF}.

Apply {FH|FGUH} equal to {AE|pAE} to {FG}. Complete the parallelepipedal solid {GK|sGK} with the same height as that of {CD|sCD} on {FH|FGUH} as base. [!just I.45; I.31]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="440" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
